WEBVTT


00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.994
This is Detective Jack Mosley.
Shield number 227.


00:00:47.171 --> 00:00:50.368
I guess this will be
my last will and testament.


00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:52.600
This is for Diane.


00:00:54.045 --> 00:00:57.640
When this day is over, they're gonna come
and talk to you about this...


00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:02.013
...and they're gonna... They're gonna
tell you what happened, Diane.


00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:05.280
But what they tell you
is not really what happened here.


00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:08.425
So I hope that you get this.


00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:14.222
I was trying to do a good thing.


00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:35.008
Police! Get down! Everybody, down!


00:01:35.186 --> 00:01:37.313
Down! Get down!


00:01:38.256 --> 00:01:40.486
Go, go, go! Come on!


00:01:41.592 --> 00:01:42.820
- Clear.
- Police. Get down.


00:01:42.994 --> 00:01:44.359
Seal it off.


00:01:44.996 --> 00:01:47.362
Agent 10-10, we're all secure.


00:01:48.366 --> 00:01:49.890
All right, we're out of here.


00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:51.558
It's clear.


00:01:53.271 --> 00:01:54.898
You smell that?


00:02:04.115 --> 00:02:07.278
Couple hours. We gotta move now.
Would you turn that thing off?


00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:09.716
All right, who's downstairs
we don't need?


00:02:27.472 --> 00:02:29.531
It's all yours. Good luck.


00:02:30.908 --> 00:02:34.537
I hate to do this, Jack, but I need you
to sit on this until uniforms get here.


00:02:34.712 --> 00:02:37.044
- All right.
- Just hang until you're relieved.


00:02:37.215 --> 00:02:38.705
All right.


00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.209
Don't touch anything.


00:03:49.821 --> 00:03:52.051
Any word on the suspects?


00:04:00.765 --> 00:04:03.461
- What do you want me to tell you?
- What did you tell them?


00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.727
I saw someone out there.


00:04:06.604 --> 00:04:07.832
Yeah, yeah. Come on.


00:04:15.279 --> 00:04:17.975
- Anything for me?
- Breath mints.


00:04:18.149 --> 00:04:22.051
Sergeant Cannova called.
Wants you to write up this wire request.


00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.654
Said to make sure
you get the right dates on them.


00:04:24.822 --> 00:04:28.417
The particulars are on your desk,
and he needs it by tonight.


00:04:29.827 --> 00:04:31.454
All right.


00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:37.061
All right, well, we can have an officer
come by about 8 a. m. Tomorrow.


00:04:47.211 --> 00:04:48.974
You gave her two?


00:04:57.388 --> 00:04:59.583
Well, you know, we do what we can.


00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:06.220
Hey, Jack, I forgot to tell you,
the lieutenant's looking for you.


00:05:06.397 --> 00:05:08.365
He wants you to find him right away.


00:05:08.833 --> 00:05:10.994
Yeah, yeah.


00:05:11.602 --> 00:05:13.866
Well, listen.
All right, well, I'll call you.


00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:19.601
Hey, Mosley.


00:05:20.912 --> 00:05:22.402
- Mosley.
- Yeah.


00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.514
Grace tell you to find me?


00:05:25.216 --> 00:05:28.652
- Yeah, just a minute ago.
- All right, need a favor.


00:05:28.819 --> 00:05:31.447
Get this guy from lockup
and run him to Centre Street.


00:05:31.622 --> 00:05:35.353
The DA needs him ASAP. He's gotta be
in front of a grand jury before 10.


00:05:36.494 --> 00:05:38.121
I signed out.


00:05:38.796 --> 00:05:40.024
You signed the sheet?


00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:43.729
Well, not technically, no.
But I mean, I'm signed out.


00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.493
Then consider yourself on overtime.


00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.968
Captain Gruber called.
We need this thing done.


00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:50.300
Don't you got some mutt
that takes care of this?


00:05:50.474 --> 00:05:54.205
I got Keenan, but he's still on the Verrazano.
He's behind some overturned truck.


00:05:58.783 --> 00:06:02.480
I'm tired. I mean, look, normally,
you know me, I don't say no.


00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:04.644
I know you been
working all night, Jack...


00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:07.416
.. but who's the detective
and who's the lieutenant here?


00:06:07.592 --> 00:06:09.856
I mean, Jack, I got nobody else.


00:06:10.027 --> 00:06:11.961
It's a nothing thing.


00:06:12.129 --> 00:06:15.587
One hundred and eighteen minutes
to get a little hemorrhoid 16 blocks.


00:06:17.802 --> 00:06:20.635
I'll let you come in
to work late tomorrow.


00:06:20.938 --> 00:06:22.496
Yeah, yeah.


00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:53.161
Edward Bunker.


00:06:53.337 --> 00:06:55.828
Yeah, that's me, officer.
Eddie Bunker, right here.


00:06:56.007 --> 00:06:57.167
Down here, the last cell.


00:06:57.341 --> 00:07:00.003
- Come back in an hour.
- What do you mean, come back?


00:07:00.177 --> 00:07:02.304
He's supposed to wear a suit
when he leaves.


00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.778
- And?
- It's not here yet.


00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:07.349
Just get him out here, all right?


00:07:07.518 --> 00:07:09.247
They said he'd wear a suit.


00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:13.322
No, yeah, I'm supposed to get a suit.
It's a three-piece suit. It's gray.


00:07:13.491 --> 00:07:14.890
It's got... Wait. Yeah.


00:07:15.059 --> 00:07:18.051
It's a three-button, it's gray,
it's got cuffs on the pants.


00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:21.062
They brought the catalog down.
I picked it out of the catalog.


00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:23.200
I'm not supposed
to leave without it. Wait.


00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:25.460
I'm not supposed to leave
without that suit.


00:07:25.636 --> 00:07:29.299
- You tell it to him.
- No, that's why you brought my shoelaces.


00:07:29.473 --> 00:07:31.270
- Come on, come on.
- I'm not supposed to.


00:07:31.442 --> 00:07:34.411
- Yo, yo, you take the old lady, right?
- Yeah, you sure?


00:07:34.578 --> 00:07:36.910
The old lady goes into the car,
otherwise she dies.


00:07:37.081 --> 00:07:38.309
- You think so?
- Yeah, man.


00:07:38.482 --> 00:07:42.248
That's what... I don't know. You gotta
figure out the answer for yourself.


00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:46.083
Everybody just calm down.
Officer, I'm going to court.


00:07:46.257 --> 00:07:47.884
- I'm supposed to have a suit.
- Hey.


00:07:48.059 --> 00:07:50.254
Shut up. Here's your property.


00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:52.692
- It's not a good sign.
- Hands behind your back.


00:07:52.863 --> 00:07:55.024
- Hold on, I'm trying...
- Hands behind your back.


00:07:55.199 --> 00:07:59.431
I don't even have my...
All my prop... Wait one minute.


00:08:00.538 --> 00:08:02.563
It's not right.
They promised me the suit.


00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:04.867
I picked it out of the catalog...
Wait, my book.


00:08:05.042 --> 00:08:08.136
I can't leave without my book.
My book is very important to me.


00:08:08.612 --> 00:08:11.342
Why are we rushing like this?
Lt's not a good sign.


00:08:11.515 --> 00:08:13.540
- Hey.
- What's the damn answer?


00:08:13.718 --> 00:08:16.084
- Hey!
- Shut up.


00:08:16.854 --> 00:08:19.721
- I hate police.
- Half a tank.


00:08:24.395 --> 00:08:26.522
You could have had
a little more patience.


00:08:26.697 --> 00:08:30.064
This suit don't mean nothing to you.
You probably got a bunch of suits.


00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:32.930
But it's a whole different thing to me.


00:08:45.116 --> 00:08:47.243
These cars don't ever change, huh?


00:08:47.985 --> 00:08:50.476
Traditional cruisers.


00:08:50.654 --> 00:08:53.623
And the same retarded hump
in the middle.


00:08:53.924 --> 00:08:58.088
Smell the same way,
like Lysol and vomit.


00:08:59.063 --> 00:09:02.396
I hope nobody vomited back here.
They probably did.


00:09:09.607 --> 00:09:12.804
Hey, man, let me ask you something.


00:09:14.044 --> 00:09:16.308
I'm trying to figure this out.


00:09:16.747 --> 00:09:19.511
You driving along
in your hurricane, right?


00:09:19.683 --> 00:09:22.049
There's three people at the bus stop.


00:09:22.219 --> 00:09:25.245
Yeah, one is an old lady.
She's sick, she about to die.


00:09:26.457 --> 00:09:29.017
The second one is your best friend.


00:09:29.193 --> 00:09:31.320
He saved your life, right?


00:09:31.495 --> 00:09:34.862
And the third is the girl of your dreams.


00:09:35.032 --> 00:09:37.023
Right, but check it out...


00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:41.494
.. you only got space in the car
for one person.


00:09:42.273 --> 00:09:44.707
Right? Who you take?


00:09:44.875 --> 00:09:48.072
Lt's a riddle that's supposed to tell
what type of person you are...


00:09:48.245 --> 00:09:49.837
.. like where you at in your life.


00:09:50.014 --> 00:09:52.574
It's a hypothetical question, man, damn.


00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.082
It's just a hypothetical...


00:09:55.252 --> 00:09:58.881
Well, good. Fine, good.
I guess that's my answer.


00:10:08.165 --> 00:10:09.826
Why don't you get
on the loudspeaker?


00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.867
Put the Hawaii Five-0 light on
or something.


00:10:13.037 --> 00:10:16.165
Use your police power.
Put on a little siren.


00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.137
Make room, make a hole.


00:10:18.309 --> 00:10:21.176
Isn't that the saying,
"Make a hole, make a hole"?


00:10:22.479 --> 00:10:24.470
Go on, make a hole.


00:10:28.552 --> 00:10:33.319
Signs. Everywhere, signs, signs, signs.
All over, man.


00:10:33.858 --> 00:10:35.985
I used to not even see
nothing like that, man.


00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.597
And then I start seeing them.
And I start looking for them.


00:10:40.965 --> 00:10:43.195
And everything just start falling in place.


00:10:45.035 --> 00:10:48.436
I'm gonna be all right,
where I'm supposed to be.


00:10:48.973 --> 00:10:52.636
I ain't got my suit,
but once they get my testimony...


00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.176
.. they drop my charges, I'm free.


00:10:55.346 --> 00:10:56.779
It's making sense to me.


00:10:57.281 --> 00:10:59.112
I believe in that.


00:10:59.283 --> 00:11:00.944
Being in the right place.


00:11:01.118 --> 00:11:03.951
Being where you supposed to be.
You believe in that?


00:11:04.121 --> 00:11:07.113
I believe life's too long
and guys like you make it even longer.


00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.427
Life's too long?


00:11:13.197 --> 00:11:14.459
Damn.


00:11:15.866 --> 00:11:19.563
That's some cold shit, man. I ain't never
heard nobody say no shit like that.


00:11:19.737 --> 00:11:23.867
Usually you hear about people
trying to make their life longer, you know?


00:11:24.041 --> 00:11:27.602
Trying to stay alive a little longer.
You sound a little...


00:11:27.778 --> 00:11:30.076
.. depressed or something, you all right?


00:11:34.051 --> 00:11:35.541
You stopping?


00:11:36.186 --> 00:11:38.313
This ain't the courthouse, man.
What you doing?


00:11:40.024 --> 00:11:41.548
Yo.


00:11:42.526 --> 00:11:44.118
Yo, why you stopping?


00:11:44.295 --> 00:11:47.628
You gonna rush me out to court,
and now you stopping? What are you...?


00:11:47.798 --> 00:11:49.959
Hey. Hey, man.


00:11:50.134 --> 00:11:54.935
Hey, man. Listen, man, I got an important
appointment after my court date, man.


00:11:55.572 --> 00:11:58.871
That shit ain't funny, man.
Come on, man. It's not a game, man.


00:11:59.043 --> 00:12:00.601
Yo.


00:12:00.945 --> 00:12:03.470
Some bullshit, man.


00:12:04.214 --> 00:12:07.445
Hey. Hey!


00:12:08.118 --> 00:12:11.178
No, man. It ain't Miller Time, man.


00:12:15.759 --> 00:12:19.422
The weather will be clear early morning,
but the rest of the day...


00:12:19.596 --> 00:12:21.496
Sam. Hey, Angela.


00:12:22.599 --> 00:12:25.067
So we are looking at a hot, humid day.


00:12:25.235 --> 00:12:27.499
Looks like temperature
might reach 100 degrees...


00:12:27.671 --> 00:12:29.571
...so don't forget
to pack your sunscreen.


00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.435
Add a pack of these, will you?


00:12:31.608 --> 00:12:35.135
I know this dude smelled funny.
I got the wrong dude, man.


00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.278
17.50. What?


00:12:38.449 --> 00:12:41.748
Hey, don't open it. Come over here.


00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.617
What time is it, man?


00:12:44.788 --> 00:12:46.551
Lt's 8:11.


00:12:49.793 --> 00:12:52.023
That's a good sign. That's a good sign.


00:12:52.196 --> 00:12:53.993
I'm on my way. I'm gonna get there.


00:12:57.101 --> 00:12:59.262
- Want change?
- No, you keep the change.


00:12:59.436 --> 00:13:01.927
Keep the change.
All right, you have a good day.


00:13:02.106 --> 00:13:04.404
- I don't want the peanuts.
- Bye.


00:13:04.875 --> 00:13:07.002
No, man. Can't do nothing for you,
understand?


00:13:07.177 --> 00:13:10.738
Hey, you better give me that change.
I'm gonna need that.


00:13:10.914 --> 00:13:12.472
You see my situation right here?


00:13:12.649 --> 00:13:14.014
No, no, no! No, no, no!


00:13:51.021 --> 00:13:52.318
Hey!


00:14:35.299 --> 00:14:37.233
How am I supposed to get out?


00:14:38.735 --> 00:14:40.225
- Come on.
- Help me. Help me.


00:14:44.141 --> 00:14:49.078
- My book. Why did you stop?
- Go, left, go. Left.


00:14:49.246 --> 00:14:52.113
Move. Move. Move.


00:14:52.282 --> 00:14:54.944
Wait. Freeze!


00:14:55.119 --> 00:14:57.383
In here. Come on.


00:15:02.059 --> 00:15:03.617
Shit.


00:15:04.761 --> 00:15:05.750
Hey!


00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.989
Just get out of here, now!
Go on. Go!


00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:13.162
Come on, let's go.
That way, let's go. Go, go.


00:15:21.578 --> 00:15:22.806
Ready? Here.


00:15:28.018 --> 00:15:30.043
Let's go. Go.


00:15:30.888 --> 00:15:34.483
- Dominic, get people out of here, right now.
- Jesus, Jackie. What's going on?


00:15:34.658 --> 00:15:36.956
- Everybody. You too.
- All right, okay.


00:15:38.795 --> 00:15:40.763
- Let's go.
- Come on, come on, come on.


00:15:42.699 --> 00:15:44.428
Hey, yo.


00:15:47.371 --> 00:15:50.568
Come on, keep going. Come on.
Come on, move it.


00:15:51.308 --> 00:15:56.245
Yeah, this is Detective Jack Mosley,
shield number 227.


00:15:56.413 --> 00:15:59.678
I am 10-13, at... Hold on a minute.


00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.843
- Dominic, what's the address here?
- 133 Mulberry.


00:16:04.021 --> 00:16:05.921
133 Mulberry.


00:16:07.658 --> 00:16:09.683
Mulberry Street.


00:16:11.361 --> 00:16:12.760
All right.


00:16:21.972 --> 00:16:23.200
Is they coming?


00:16:28.078 --> 00:16:30.808
I don't know why you stopped, man.


00:16:31.315 --> 00:16:34.113
I don't know why
you would do that, man.


00:16:36.853 --> 00:16:38.081
They said you were nobody.


00:16:38.255 --> 00:16:40.985
- I ain't nobody.
- Shut up.


00:16:41.158 --> 00:16:44.127
You a wino. You need to stop drinking,
that's what you need.


00:16:44.294 --> 00:16:47.457
Shut up.


00:16:58.508 --> 00:16:59.941
Jack?


00:17:01.979 --> 00:17:03.810
- Frank.
- Hey.


00:17:04.147 --> 00:17:05.842
You all right?


00:17:07.084 --> 00:17:08.574
- Yeah.
- Yeah?


00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:12.550
We were on Mott when the call went out.
Heard it was you.


00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.821
Got here as soon as we could.


00:17:19.096 --> 00:17:20.961
Oh, hi.


00:17:21.698 --> 00:17:23.666
- Hey.
- You all right?


00:17:23.834 --> 00:17:26.302
- Yeah, I'm all right.
- You having fun?


00:17:27.404 --> 00:17:29.429
- No.
- No? Oh, well.


00:17:29.906 --> 00:17:31.771
Gotta have fun.


00:17:36.079 --> 00:17:39.480
- What's up, Jack?
- Hey, man. Hi.


00:17:40.584 --> 00:17:44.782
You did a really great, great job, man.


00:17:44.955 --> 00:17:47.150
You got yourself a bad guy.


00:17:48.091 --> 00:17:50.685
Been a while, huh? Yeah.


00:17:50.861 --> 00:17:56.026
We got the second shooter
half a block from here, so it's done.


00:17:59.303 --> 00:18:00.668
- Sure you're okay?
- Yeah.


00:18:00.837 --> 00:18:04.295
I'm just getting my wind. I was running.


00:18:04.875 --> 00:18:06.843
Why don't you let us take it from here.


00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.308
Oh, yeah.


00:18:09.479 --> 00:18:14.041
We'll get the kid where he belongs,
and you don't have to worry about a thing.


00:18:14.451 --> 00:18:16.442
- We'll get you home.
- Yes, please.


00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.180
Please, please, officer.
That's a very good idea...


00:18:19.356 --> 00:18:22.291
.. because, honestly, I don't think
this dude is doing too good.


00:18:22.459 --> 00:18:23.687
I told him not to stop.


00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:26.351
I asked him not to stop.
He just had to stop.


00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:29.226
That's when everything happened.
Dude came to the window.


00:18:29.399 --> 00:18:31.890
I have a very important
appointment aft...


00:18:32.069 --> 00:18:33.502
Jack.


00:18:34.504 --> 00:18:35.869
Hey, Shue.


00:18:45.082 --> 00:18:46.572
Come on. Here.


00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.274
Why don't you take this. Come on.


00:18:48.452 --> 00:18:51.046
We'll get you out of here.
Got a car waiting. All right?


00:18:51.221 --> 00:18:52.654
Get some sleep.


00:18:56.126 --> 00:18:57.650
Jack?


00:19:28.291 --> 00:19:32.091
The kid was gonna testify against Jerry.


00:19:33.096 --> 00:19:36.259
He saw Jerry doing some business.


00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:41.298
Now, we both know that Jerry has never
been a standup guy like you and me.


00:19:42.839 --> 00:19:47.299
He'll roll over, they indict him.
We can't have that.


00:19:47.477 --> 00:19:51.072
No. It's gonna hurt a lot of us.


00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.449
Come on.


00:20:05.295 --> 00:20:09.959
See, this whole thing caught us...
It caught us completely unaware.


00:20:13.236 --> 00:20:16.034
It was supposed to be
Teach's nephew driving him.


00:20:16.206 --> 00:20:19.733
But he got stuck out there in traffic,
who knows where...


00:20:20.877 --> 00:20:22.902
.. so then your lieutenant, he pegged you.


00:20:24.614 --> 00:20:29.142
You know, just the wrong time
and the wrong place for you today.


00:20:30.654 --> 00:20:35.921
All right. Now, you know that I would never
put you in a position like this, right?


00:20:36.092 --> 00:20:38.117
You know that, huh?


00:20:38.295 --> 00:20:41.321
And I never figured
you'd cap one of those guys.


00:20:41.798 --> 00:20:45.063
- That's what I get for hiring drug addicts.
- Grab the gun.


00:20:47.571 --> 00:20:51.132
Grab the gun. There you go.


00:20:52.509 --> 00:20:53.635
Come on. Frank?


00:20:55.212 --> 00:20:57.874
- Here we go.
- All right, here we go. Jack.


00:20:58.982 --> 00:21:00.347
Squeeze the trigger.


00:21:03.587 --> 00:21:08.286
All right. Let go of the gun.
Let go of the gun.


00:21:12.496 --> 00:21:13.827
I figure it like this.


00:21:14.664 --> 00:21:18.862
You... You pop the guys
trying to spring the kid.


00:21:19.035 --> 00:21:21.799
The kid, well, he gets your gun.


00:21:22.572 --> 00:21:24.597
And he takes you hostage.


00:21:24.774 --> 00:21:28.210
So we came in and saved the day.


00:21:28.378 --> 00:21:30.676
He died, you lived.


00:21:32.048 --> 00:21:35.142
Now, this could be a good thing
for you, Jack.


00:21:37.487 --> 00:21:39.717
Get you back where you belong.


00:21:48.865 --> 00:21:50.526
- Are you still with?
- Stand up.


00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:53.100
- You still with what's-her-name?
- Come on, stand up.


00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:56.561
- What are you waiting for?
- What's her name?


00:22:13.123 --> 00:22:14.852
Caroline.


00:22:15.926 --> 00:22:17.723
It's Caroline.


00:22:19.829 --> 00:22:21.922
This changes everything, Jack.


00:22:25.268 --> 00:22:26.758
Over here.


00:22:31.708 --> 00:22:33.335
Come on, Frank.


00:22:37.948 --> 00:22:41.884
Kid, get up. Come on.


00:22:47.524 --> 00:22:49.822
Shit. Man, shit.


00:22:53.897 --> 00:22:57.890
All right, Jack, it's 8:25.


00:22:58.702 --> 00:23:02.798
- You stay there.
- Listen to me, the jury's tenure ends at 10.


00:23:02.973 --> 00:23:06.670
All right? The kid gets there
one minute past, all this...


00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.709
.. it doesn't matter.


00:23:13.249 --> 00:23:15.649
And all you gotta do
is look the other way.


00:23:15.819 --> 00:23:17.753
All right? We still got options here.


00:23:17.921 --> 00:23:19.218
Okay?


00:23:19.389 --> 00:23:20.617
We just want the kid.


00:23:23.093 --> 00:23:26.290
Jack, Jack, Jack,
just let me help you.


00:23:26.796 --> 00:23:27.990
All right?


00:23:28.164 --> 00:23:29.791
Back up.


00:23:32.602 --> 00:23:36.060
Jack, once you go out that door...


00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:38.204
.. I can't help you.


00:23:38.375 --> 00:23:41.503
Please just back up, Frank.
Just back up.


00:24:01.631 --> 00:24:03.189
He shot a cop.


00:24:03.466 --> 00:24:06.060
What the hell did you see?
What did you see?


00:24:06.236 --> 00:24:07.999
That cop back there.


00:24:08.171 --> 00:24:09.798
I seen him around my way...


00:24:09.973 --> 00:24:12.999
.. holding a gun in this
little Puerto Rican kid's mouth.


00:24:13.176 --> 00:24:14.973
Come on. Let's go.


00:24:15.145 --> 00:24:18.239
He said he'd kill his mother
if he testified.


00:24:19.249 --> 00:24:21.342
What you doing that for?
We need that.


00:24:21.518 --> 00:24:24.817
The shell in that gun was over 20 years old.
Lucky it went off at all.


00:24:24.988 --> 00:24:28.048
- They didn't tell you Shue was a cop?
- No, they didn't tell me.


00:24:28.224 --> 00:24:30.317
They showed me a picture, that was it.


00:24:30.493 --> 00:24:34.554
Well, congratulations, because you're about
to testify against one of New York's worst.


00:24:34.731 --> 00:24:36.699
- What?
- Fellas, look, the clock's ticking.


00:24:36.866 --> 00:24:39.994
He's gotta be at the courthouse by 10.
We know where he's going.


00:24:40.170 --> 00:24:42.536
Mulvey, you're coming with me.


00:24:43.039 --> 00:24:45.166
- Know where you're going?
- Take the north side.


00:24:45.341 --> 00:24:46.968
- You got it, let's go.
- Come on.


00:24:47.677 --> 00:24:51.044
- Captain.
- Where are we, Frank?


00:24:51.214 --> 00:24:54.012
Well, we're putting descriptions out
over precinct channels.


00:24:54.184 --> 00:24:59.019
No names, or that one's a cop.
It'll help to have some eyes.


00:24:59.389 --> 00:25:02.085
- How long can you sit on this?
- He shot a cop.


00:25:02.559 --> 00:25:05.551
You're the precinct captain, Dan.
How long?


00:25:05.729 --> 00:25:08.789
I don't know.
Hour, maybe a little more.


00:25:09.399 --> 00:25:11.026
- Who's on this with you?
- My guys.


00:25:11.201 --> 00:25:15.399
Ortiz and Maldonado from the 66.
Touhey and Kaller from the 111.


00:25:15.572 --> 00:25:17.597
A couple others
you don't wanna know about.


00:25:21.611 --> 00:25:24.239
The guy was your partner for 20 years.


00:25:24.414 --> 00:25:26.746
What the hell happened in there?


00:25:26.916 --> 00:25:29.180
- Is he drunk?
- I don't know.


00:25:29.652 --> 00:25:31.813
I don't know. We woke him up.


00:25:32.489 --> 00:25:35.617
Hopefully he'll do what he always does,
and we can go back to work.


00:25:35.792 --> 00:25:37.657
If he doesn't?


00:25:40.296 --> 00:25:44.665
We gotta quash this thing
before he gets his legs back.


00:25:45.435 --> 00:25:47.460
These are his streets.


00:25:50.206 --> 00:25:54.438
This could get ugly for all of us
if that kid talks.


00:25:54.611 --> 00:25:56.943
- He can't talk.
- He won't talk.


00:25:57.447 --> 00:25:59.915
Look, I appreciate
what you did for me back there...


00:26:00.083 --> 00:26:02.745
.. but I'm starting to think
you're not the dude for this.


00:26:02.919 --> 00:26:05.547
I mean, you're out of breath,
you're hung-over.


00:26:05.722 --> 00:26:07.986
Your leg is gonna give out on you
any second, man.


00:26:08.158 --> 00:26:11.457
I got someplace I need to be at 12,
you understand?


00:26:11.628 --> 00:26:13.528
I need to be finished at court by 10...


00:26:13.696 --> 00:26:16.096
.. or I'm not gonna get
where I'm supposed to get.


00:26:16.266 --> 00:26:19.133
- You understand what I'm saying?
- All right, I understand.


00:26:19.302 --> 00:26:22.738
- You're not listening to what I'm saying.
- Wait, come here. Come here.


00:26:27.443 --> 00:26:28.933
Come on.


00:26:30.547 --> 00:26:32.378
Hung-over.


00:26:32.549 --> 00:26:34.346
A bad leg.


00:26:34.517 --> 00:26:36.314
No gun.


00:26:39.989 --> 00:26:41.684
- Bobby?
- Yeah?


00:26:41.858 --> 00:26:44.691
- You thinking what I'm thinking?
- I'm already there.


00:27:09.319 --> 00:27:11.184
Oh, God.


00:27:15.058 --> 00:27:16.855
Come on, let's go.


00:27:17.026 --> 00:27:21.725
Listen, just stay put right here.
I'll be right back.


00:27:25.001 --> 00:27:27.231
Come on, man, don't take long.
We gotta go.


00:27:29.739 --> 00:27:31.331
Hurry up.


00:27:32.342 --> 00:27:35.277
- Hey, man, where your bathroom?
- What?


00:27:35.445 --> 00:27:37.310
Your bathroom. Where your bathroom at?


00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:39.675
Down at the end of the hall.


00:27:40.049 --> 00:27:41.516
Yeah.


00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:46.646
That's what you look like
when you smile, huh?


00:27:47.457 --> 00:27:49.755
You was probably drinking then too.


00:27:53.596 --> 00:27:55.564
There's the lady.


00:27:56.366 --> 00:27:59.358
Redhead. She cute. That ain't bad.


00:27:59.535 --> 00:28:02.800
Hey, man. Come on, don't be stopping
to get high or nothing like that.


00:28:02.972 --> 00:28:04.837
Man, we gotta go.


00:28:07.043 --> 00:28:09.944
Make sure you lift the seat up
before you go.


00:28:13.383 --> 00:28:15.112
It's up already.


00:28:17.453 --> 00:28:20.115
Maybe you left it like that, huh?


00:29:00.930 --> 00:29:02.522
I'm coming.


00:29:18.181 --> 00:29:19.910
Hey, Jack.


00:29:21.284 --> 00:29:22.546
Jack Mosley.


00:29:26.456 --> 00:29:27.718
Why did you do that?


00:29:29.258 --> 00:29:30.782
Do what?


00:29:31.260 --> 00:29:33.228
Shoot that cop.


00:29:34.998 --> 00:29:36.522
Cops...


00:29:36.799 --> 00:29:38.357
.. they don't shoot other cops.


00:29:41.371 --> 00:29:43.703
Especially over nobody like me.


00:29:55.351 --> 00:29:58.411
It's a long way to go for a stranger,
you know.


00:30:00.089 --> 00:30:01.681
Thank you.


00:30:02.392 --> 00:30:04.690
I never had nobody...


00:30:04.861 --> 00:30:06.692
Hell, man, you know.


00:30:06.863 --> 00:30:10.458
I don't rock with the police,
you know what I'm saying?


00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:13.167
- Finger off the trigger.
- They never been my friend.


00:30:13.336 --> 00:30:15.065
- Then here you come.
- On the ground.


00:30:15.238 --> 00:30:17.138
It's kind of bugging me out, you know.


00:30:18.107 --> 00:30:20.974
You on some vigilante business.


00:30:21.144 --> 00:30:22.611
Let's go.


00:30:24.347 --> 00:30:26.406
- Jack...
- Put your arms around the pole.


00:30:26.582 --> 00:30:28.174
I don't know what to think anymore.


00:30:28.351 --> 00:30:31.650
- Here. Cuff yourself.
- What are you doing, Jack?


00:30:31.821 --> 00:30:34.813
Yeah, it's a little strange.


00:30:34.991 --> 00:30:37.459
You know? By any definition, this here.


00:30:37.627 --> 00:30:39.390
All right, kid. Good.


00:30:39.562 --> 00:30:41.120
Okay.


00:30:41.330 --> 00:30:44.993
Okay, okay, okay.


00:30:45.368 --> 00:30:47.097
Okay.


00:30:48.304 --> 00:30:49.635
Okay.


00:30:50.673 --> 00:30:53.403
You should have done
what you always do, Jack.


00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:58.111
- Where's your phone?
- It's on the left-hand side.


00:30:59.248 --> 00:31:01.978
They know I'm here.
If I don't answer it...


00:31:05.621 --> 00:31:07.589
- Jack?
- Let's go, kid. Come on.


00:31:21.771 --> 00:31:25.104
- Bob.
- Bob's a little tied up right now, Frank.


00:31:25.875 --> 00:31:27.399
All right, I'm impressed, Jack.


00:31:27.577 --> 00:31:28.703
Did you shoot him too?


00:31:30.947 --> 00:31:33.347
Send someone to check on Bobby.


00:31:38.621 --> 00:31:40.248
Jack, you're not up to this.


00:31:40.556 --> 00:31:42.319
All right? It's gonna end bad for you.


00:31:46.095 --> 00:31:48.586
You lost the kid, didn't you?


00:31:50.500 --> 00:31:52.434
He bailed on you. Well, you know what?


00:31:52.602 --> 00:31:54.763
That is the best thing
that could have happened.


00:31:54.937 --> 00:31:56.268
So why don't you go home.


00:31:56.439 --> 00:31:57.667
Forget about what happened.


00:31:57.840 --> 00:32:00.365
We'll take it from here.
Are you looking for him?


00:32:00.543 --> 00:32:02.272
And you can't find him.


00:32:02.445 --> 00:32:04.538
We're gonna find him, all right?


00:32:05.081 --> 00:32:06.309
We're gonna find him.


00:32:06.482 --> 00:32:09.212
All right, Jack, now you can hang up.


00:32:13.089 --> 00:32:14.954
Where are you, kid?


00:32:15.391 --> 00:32:17.951
All right. Now, let's see
which way he went.


00:32:18.127 --> 00:32:20.721
Did he go up? Did he go down?


00:32:20.897 --> 00:32:23.331
In or out, Jackie.
Which way did he go?


00:32:25.668 --> 00:32:28.068
Let's see if he went down.


00:32:29.772 --> 00:32:32.332
- Excuse me, sir, do you mind swiping?
- Get a job, man.


00:32:32.508 --> 00:32:34.237
Ma'am, would you mind swiping me in?


00:32:34.410 --> 00:32:37.402
Ma'am? Ma'am, would you mind
swiping me in, please, ma'am?


00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:40.640
I have a very important
appointment I have to...


00:32:43.219 --> 00:32:46.347
Excuse me, ma'am, would you mind...?
Somebody mind swiping me in?


00:32:46.522 --> 00:32:49.753
I'm trying to get
to an important appointment.


00:32:49.926 --> 00:32:52.588
Somebody help me. Somebody help me.


00:32:52.762 --> 00:32:54.957
Somebody help me.


00:32:55.464 --> 00:32:56.897
Hey.


00:32:58.901 --> 00:33:00.266
Come here.


00:33:01.103 --> 00:33:04.038
- Come on. Go.
- Thank you. Thank you very much.


00:33:19.155 --> 00:33:20.645
Eddie!


00:33:20.823 --> 00:33:22.256
- Oh, no.
- What are you doing?


00:33:22.425 --> 00:33:24.256
- Why are you running?
- What do you want?


00:33:24.427 --> 00:33:26.691
Lt's too much, man.
I'm doing the rest on my own.


00:33:26.862 --> 00:33:29.194
I'm doing what I said.
I'm getting out of here.


00:33:29.365 --> 00:33:32.562
- Lf I can find you, they can find you!
- I'm doing what I said.


00:33:33.069 --> 00:33:35.765
Eddie, listen to me. Listen to me.
Listen to me!


00:33:35.938 --> 00:33:38.805
- I'm your only friend down here.
- No, you're not my friend.


00:33:38.975 --> 00:33:42.206
- I can do this...
- Friend? You don't even know me!


00:33:42.378 --> 00:33:44.744
And get me where?
You gonna get me shot.


00:33:45.014 --> 00:33:48.643
Ever since I've been with you, people been
trying to shoot me. People you know!


00:33:48.818 --> 00:33:52.083
Look, man, I got someplace I need to be.
I got something I need to do.


00:33:52.255 --> 00:33:54.951
Unless you gonna shoot me or arrest me,
I'm going, Jack.


00:33:55.124 --> 00:33:58.252
- I can't let you leave.
- Thank you, Jack Mosley. I'm going.


00:33:58.427 --> 00:34:00.895
- You can't leave.
- Yes, I can. Thank you, Jack Mosley.


00:34:01.197 --> 00:34:02.789
Stop. Don't do that. Stop.


00:34:02.965 --> 00:34:05.365
Ladies and gentlemen...!
You're not going. Come here.


00:34:05.534 --> 00:34:07.502
Eddie!


00:34:09.105 --> 00:34:10.936
Okay, okay.
Okay, we gotta go.


00:34:11.107 --> 00:34:13.598
- Move! Move!
- Get out of the way!


00:34:16.579 --> 00:34:18.240
Move! Move!


00:34:27.623 --> 00:34:29.215
- Here, come on.
- What are you doing?


00:34:29.392 --> 00:34:32.020
Taxi! Hey!


00:34:32.194 --> 00:34:34.059
Taxi!


00:34:37.867 --> 00:34:40.665
Lt's Kaller. He just missed them
at the Canal Street station.


00:34:41.003 --> 00:34:42.937
Where, where, where?


00:34:43.239 --> 00:34:46.265
Shit. Where the hell is he?


00:34:46.776 --> 00:34:48.641
Goddamn it.


00:34:48.811 --> 00:34:51.006
We're gonna find you.


00:34:51.180 --> 00:34:53.774
Yeah, this is Detective Nugent.
I need a triangulation...


00:34:53.949 --> 00:34:57.976
...on Detective Torres' cell phone.
Area code 935...


00:35:01.590 --> 00:35:06.289
That cop back at the apartment,
he said you should do what you always do.


00:35:06.462 --> 00:35:09.124
What did he...?
What did he mean by that?


00:35:10.800 --> 00:35:14.099
You're not doing
what you always do, huh?


00:35:14.270 --> 00:35:17.068
Jack Mosley, I get it. I see the signs.


00:35:17.239 --> 00:35:20.572
I'm where I'm supposed to be.
I was wrong. You're the right guy.


00:35:20.743 --> 00:35:23.940
I could have got another guy,
did something different, but I got you.


00:35:24.113 --> 00:35:25.876
I appreciate it. You're the right guy.


00:35:26.048 --> 00:35:27.037
- Okay?
- Okay.


00:35:27.216 --> 00:35:29.707
- This is Comtech, over.
- Yeah, go, this is Nugent.


00:35:29.885 --> 00:35:32.979
GPS indicates they're on Bowery.


00:35:33.155 --> 00:35:35.180
Repeat, Bowery,
moving south towards Pell.


00:35:35.358 --> 00:35:36.848
Speed indicates they're on foot.


00:35:37.026 --> 00:35:39.119
Are you hearing this, boys?
He's in Chinatown.


00:35:39.495 --> 00:35:41.292
Let's move in.


00:35:49.939 --> 00:35:52.703
- What's the deal with that book?
- It's my business plans.


00:35:52.875 --> 00:35:55.639
I'm moving to Seattle.
My sister's already living out there.


00:35:55.811 --> 00:35:58.939
I'm gonna open up a bakery.
But it's only, like, a specialty bakery.


00:35:59.115 --> 00:36:02.016
Birthday cakes for little kids.
There's a lot of money in that.


00:36:02.184 --> 00:36:05.017
I'm gonna send you
a big birthday cake on your birthday...


00:36:05.187 --> 00:36:07.655
- I hate birthday cakes.
- You hate birthday cakes?


00:36:07.823 --> 00:36:09.620
First thing that doesn't go your way...


00:36:09.792 --> 00:36:12.556
.. you're gonna be slipping into
Carol's Clip and Curl...


00:36:12.728 --> 00:36:14.719
.. and stealing all her hair-care products.


00:36:14.897 --> 00:36:17.422
Because you're a thief.
And that's what you are, Eddie.


00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:21.036
- You're always gonna be a thief.
- People can change, Jack.


00:36:21.203 --> 00:36:24.195
- Days change, seasons change. Not people.
- Yes, you do...


00:36:24.373 --> 00:36:27.570
- People don't change, Eddie.
- Yes, you do. I'll get you that cake.


00:36:27.743 --> 00:36:29.404
You know what it's gonna say on top?


00:36:29.578 --> 00:36:33.480
"Jack Mosley, ha-ha-ha, eat this. " Make you
eat your words, lick your fingers too.


00:36:33.649 --> 00:36:35.310
Subject's moving west on Pell.


00:36:38.554 --> 00:36:42.081
Subject now moving south on Doyers.
Still moving south on Doyers.


00:36:42.258 --> 00:36:45.819
Bobby, you take Doyer, we got Pell.
And, Kaller, you close up Bowery.


00:36:45.995 --> 00:36:47.394
- Copy that.
- Let's squeeze him.


00:36:47.563 --> 00:36:50.498
- Copy that, on my way.
- Why don't you pull up. Pull up.


00:37:33.375 --> 00:37:35.434
- Sorry.
- Who is that? You can't go in here.


00:37:35.611 --> 00:37:37.010
Oh, sorry.


00:37:56.599 --> 00:38:00.660
Look, man, I gotta be down there.
All right, you understand?


00:38:01.070 --> 00:38:04.938
I gotta be down there that way, and
there's streets and shit in between there.


00:38:05.107 --> 00:38:08.702
You got some sort of plan?
Some sort of police plan or something?


00:38:08.878 --> 00:38:11.676
I see your limp acting up.
You ought to get that checked out.


00:38:11.847 --> 00:38:15.476
I have a buddy of mine
walking around with a limp just like that.


00:38:15.651 --> 00:38:17.915
He don't wanna go
to the doctor, though, right?


00:38:18.087 --> 00:38:21.682
Finally he go,
they say it's a fracture, right?


00:38:21.857 --> 00:38:24.690
And now it's infected.
They gotta cut it off at the knee.


00:38:25.594 --> 00:38:27.653
Wasn't so bad, though.
He had no more pain.


00:38:27.830 --> 00:38:30.663
He ended up moving to Jersey,
working for the PATH...


00:38:30.833 --> 00:38:33.233
.. being a motorman.
Got a pension and shit now.


00:38:33.402 --> 00:38:36.963
I guess everything happens for a reason,
you know what I mean?


00:38:37.139 --> 00:38:39.539
You're a sunny little shit,
I'll give you that much.


00:38:45.714 --> 00:38:47.682
Get in here! Get in that door!


00:38:48.517 --> 00:38:50.178
Jack!


00:38:50.686 --> 00:38:55.555
- Pull me in! Help me in!
- Come on, come on, come on.


00:38:55.724 --> 00:38:56.816
Lock the door.


00:39:02.831 --> 00:39:04.264
- Wait, wait, wait.
- Hold up.


00:39:06.368 --> 00:39:07.596
Come on.


00:39:38.167 --> 00:39:40.294
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:39:57.019 --> 00:39:59.681
Jack, what are we doing?
Where are we going?


00:40:04.293 --> 00:40:07.228
- Come on.
- Where we going, Jack?


00:40:08.631 --> 00:40:10.121
Out of the way.


00:40:10.299 --> 00:40:11.732
Over here.


00:40:12.434 --> 00:40:16.734
Jack? How we even know that Centre Street
Courthouse is in this direction, Jack?


00:40:16.905 --> 00:40:18.532
Jack? We gotta know...


00:40:19.441 --> 00:40:21.409
Down! Head down!


00:40:22.745 --> 00:40:23.734
Go!


00:40:26.749 --> 00:40:28.740
Come on!


00:40:42.297 --> 00:40:43.696
Kaller!


00:40:45.234 --> 00:40:47.134
Push it.


00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:20.058
You all right, Jack?


00:41:24.873 --> 00:41:27.433
I was aiming for the kid,
if that makes you feel better.


00:41:27.609 --> 00:41:29.543
Well, you missed!


00:41:34.049 --> 00:41:36.643
That kid is gonna get you killed.


00:41:38.020 --> 00:41:39.885
He worth that?


00:41:46.295 --> 00:41:48.286
Well, I got all day.


00:41:49.732 --> 00:41:51.791
How about you, you got all day?


00:41:54.970 --> 00:41:58.303
- Jack, you still there?
- Yeah.


00:41:58.607 --> 00:42:00.006
Still here.


00:42:02.578 --> 00:42:04.478
Well, this is awkward.


00:42:09.418 --> 00:42:11.943
When I started this day...


00:42:12.621 --> 00:42:15.419
.. I never figured on trading
9 mils with my friend.


00:42:16.658 --> 00:42:22.392
I think we stopped being friends
right around 8:25, in that bar.


00:42:23.232 --> 00:42:24.722
No.


00:42:25.567 --> 00:42:30.504
No, that's not gonna erase
20 years together.


00:42:30.739 --> 00:42:32.104
We're still friends.


00:42:36.745 --> 00:42:38.610
Look...


00:42:39.148 --> 00:42:41.946
.. a lot I'd take back, but I can't.


00:42:42.551 --> 00:42:46.920
Well, so you move forward.
Next day, next case.


00:42:48.090 --> 00:42:50.183
- Lines were crossed.
- What lines?


00:42:50.359 --> 00:42:55.592
- You hear me? Lines were crossed, Frank.
- What lines? There are no lines!


00:42:55.931 --> 00:42:58.491
There's getting it done
and not getting it done, period!


00:42:59.201 --> 00:43:02.762
You put the bad guys away
no matter what it takes.


00:43:02.938 --> 00:43:05.463
Now, you're gonna ruin the lives...


00:43:06.008 --> 00:43:08.135
.. of six cops.


00:43:09.211 --> 00:43:10.906
Good cops.


00:43:11.079 --> 00:43:12.876
Good men.


00:43:16.018 --> 00:43:20.978
Are you ready to sacrifice
their lives for that kid?


00:43:22.024 --> 00:43:23.958
Hey, Frank.


00:43:24.259 --> 00:43:26.124
- Frank.
- Yeah?


00:43:26.295 --> 00:43:29.628
This is not about me
ruining anybody's life.


00:43:29.798 --> 00:43:32.062
Okay? This is about you.


00:43:33.202 --> 00:43:34.897
You hear me?


00:43:35.904 --> 00:43:37.496
Yeah.


00:43:38.841 --> 00:43:40.502
You look at that kid's jacket?


00:43:42.044 --> 00:43:43.671
I did.


00:43:43.879 --> 00:43:47.246
- Armed robbery, assault, beats old women...
- I never had no armed robbery!


00:43:47.416 --> 00:43:50.544
Beats old women over the heads,
steals their Social Security checks.


00:43:50.719 --> 00:43:53.711
- One time, I used...
- Shut up. Shut up.


00:43:53.889 --> 00:43:55.754
Oh, no, don't tell him to shut up.


00:43:55.924 --> 00:44:01.123
No, Jack, listen to him.
No, that kid, he's sharp.


00:44:01.296 --> 00:44:02.558
Yeah, he's playing you.


00:44:04.633 --> 00:44:06.828
He's sharper than you are.


00:44:07.569 --> 00:44:09.662
He's telling you stories, right?


00:44:10.339 --> 00:44:12.671
He wants to be a good citizen.


00:44:14.009 --> 00:44:15.237
Go to church.


00:44:15.844 --> 00:44:17.869
Buy his mother a house.


00:44:18.046 --> 00:44:21.914
But he has spent
more than half his life in prison.


00:44:23.952 --> 00:44:29.185
Two hours ago, he was sitting in a cell
for weapons possession.


00:44:29.358 --> 00:44:32.156
- He's always gonna do what he has done.
- I wasn't...


00:44:32.327 --> 00:44:35.763
He is a career criminal.
That's who you're protecting.


00:44:37.666 --> 00:44:41.102
- You all right?
- Yeah. Frank's got him on the other side.


00:44:41.803 --> 00:44:43.100
He's got my gun too.


00:44:43.505 --> 00:44:45.564
Now, if you can't see
how wrong this is...


00:44:45.741 --> 00:44:48.733
.. I promise you
I will speak from my heart...


00:44:49.778 --> 00:44:52.246
.. when I give the eulogy at your funeral.


00:44:53.415 --> 00:44:55.110
So...


00:44:56.351 --> 00:44:58.046
.. do you believe the kid?


00:45:00.856 --> 00:45:03.256
Or do you believe your ex-partner?


00:45:08.163 --> 00:45:10.723
Frank, we're right
on the other side of the door.


00:45:10.899 --> 00:45:12.662
Because...


00:45:14.036 --> 00:45:16.163
.. if you believe the kid...


00:45:18.774 --> 00:45:21.004
.. you got a choice to make.


00:45:28.951 --> 00:45:31.351
Do you go through your ex-partner?


00:45:33.288 --> 00:45:35.085
Or do you choose door number two...


00:45:35.490 --> 00:45:40.826
.. and go back to where you came,
with your gimpy leg and your shot-up hand?


00:45:49.137 --> 00:45:53.471
You're not gonna get very far.
And what if your ex-partner is right, Jack?


00:45:54.343 --> 00:45:57.369
What if he is right, and you're wasting
your whole miserable life?


00:46:17.566 --> 00:46:18.794
- It's Frank.
- You all right?


00:46:18.967 --> 00:46:21.629
Yeah. They're in the elevator.
Seal the building.


00:46:22.371 --> 00:46:24.202
Come on, Bobby.
Come on, get on that.


00:46:25.007 --> 00:46:26.372
Everybody out! Police!


00:46:27.509 --> 00:46:31.741
Everybody out! Police!
Move, move! Police!


00:46:32.914 --> 00:46:35.883
- Frank, where are you?
- Bobby, I'm coming up!


00:46:37.052 --> 00:46:40.180
All right. Come on, come on.
Upstairs. Seal the stairwell.


00:46:40.355 --> 00:46:42.687
- All right.
- Find the back stairs. Check the roof.


00:46:42.858 --> 00:46:44.416
- Come on, Mal! This way.
- Got you.


00:46:44.593 --> 00:46:46.959
- Maldonado, seal it up.
- Got you.


00:47:02.677 --> 00:47:06.044
Hello? Hello? Hello?


00:47:10.118 --> 00:47:13.576
- No, nothing.
- No answer. He's not there. Come on.


00:47:21.663 --> 00:47:24.097
I never open door.


00:47:24.266 --> 00:47:27.497
Please. Please, help.


00:47:29.905 --> 00:47:31.202
Come on.


00:47:35.077 --> 00:47:37.477
Jack, Jack, Jack. Thank you.


00:47:39.581 --> 00:47:42.049
- Thank you. Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.


00:47:42.217 --> 00:47:46.677
- You saw that, right? You heard him, right?
- Yeah. He never opens the door.


00:47:56.064 --> 00:47:59.033
Thank you very much, sir. Thank you.


00:47:59.701 --> 00:48:01.931
- Thank you. Thank you very much, sir.
- Thank you.


00:48:02.104 --> 00:48:05.267
- You heard him, right, Jack?
- Not now, Eddie.


00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:08.603
- Keep your voice down.
- He said he never opens the door.


00:48:08.777 --> 00:48:11.268
You know what that mean, right?


00:48:13.815 --> 00:48:15.806
Not right now.
There's the signs everywhere.


00:48:15.984 --> 00:48:19.920
- Yeah, ADA MacDonald, please.
- May I tell her who's calling?


00:48:20.088 --> 00:48:22.522
Yeah, tell her it's the guy
that's got her witness.


00:48:29.464 --> 00:48:33.059
You're driving a car
during a hurricane.


00:48:33.235 --> 00:48:34.759
Like:


00:48:34.936 --> 00:48:36.961
A hurricane.


00:48:37.139 --> 00:48:40.199
And there's three people at a bus stop.


00:48:40.375 --> 00:48:42.843
- A old woman.
- Yeah.


00:48:43.011 --> 00:48:46.003
A friend, like my friend here.


00:48:46.414 --> 00:48:49.383
Him. He save your life, your friend.


00:48:49.818 --> 00:48:52.651
It's Detective Mosley for you.


00:48:52.821 --> 00:48:53.981
- Mosley?
- Yeah?


00:48:54.156 --> 00:48:55.953
Where are you?
Where's my witness?


00:48:56.124 --> 00:48:57.887
I'm about seven blocks from you.


00:48:58.059 --> 00:49:00.391
But there's about a ton of cops
between me and you.


00:49:00.562 --> 00:49:02.291
And they all want this kid dead.


00:49:02.464 --> 00:49:04.955
Not to mention that
you got a leak in your office.


00:49:05.133 --> 00:49:08.227
- Somebody's talking to these cops.
- Shit.


00:49:08.403 --> 00:49:11.065
What did you think was gonna happen
when you pinched Shue?


00:49:11.239 --> 00:49:13.707
You thought they'd just lay down
and go away quietly?


00:49:13.875 --> 00:49:16.469
We thought if we went to the grand jury,
Shue would fold.


00:49:16.645 --> 00:49:17.873
He bent but didn't break.


00:49:18.046 --> 00:49:21.538
We were gonna throw it away until
we ran into Edward Bunker last night.


00:49:21.983 --> 00:49:26.181
Jury's tenure ends at 10. Without that kid,
they'll vote no bill and it all goes away.


00:49:26.354 --> 00:49:28.584
He's an eyewitness.
He makes this work.


00:49:28.757 --> 00:49:31.487
Where are you? I'll send my squad.
Richard, pen.


00:49:49.711 --> 00:49:51.008
What room?


00:49:56.418 --> 00:50:00.616
- So, what, are they coming?
- Yeah, they're coming.


00:50:00.989 --> 00:50:06.222
Good. Because I gotta be somewhere, man.
I got something to do.


00:50:06.394 --> 00:50:09.625
I gotta be someplace by noon.
I gotta go get something.


00:50:09.798 --> 00:50:11.732
It's real important.


00:50:12.367 --> 00:50:13.459
- Oh, shit.
- Yeah.


00:50:14.369 --> 00:50:16.735
Ortiz, I'm coming in the building.


00:50:18.373 --> 00:50:19.965
Frank?


00:50:23.044 --> 00:50:27.208
- Touhey and Kaller are taken care of.
- Good. Find Bobby. He's on the back stairs.


00:50:27.382 --> 00:50:30.112
Eddie, come here, put this on.
Here, come on, put that on.


00:50:30.285 --> 00:50:33.743
But it's a big, hot, wool shirt.
It's hot. It's summer.


00:50:33.922 --> 00:50:36.550
- You're dressed like a criminal.
- Oh, you want me to...?


00:50:36.725 --> 00:50:39.785
You want me to change my...?
I get it. But why can't I put that on?


00:50:39.961 --> 00:50:41.553
- What about this?
- What about that?


00:50:41.730 --> 00:50:44.995
- What's wrong with this? Lt's just a pattern.
- He don't even wear that.


00:50:45.166 --> 00:50:46.497
Just put the... Here.


00:50:46.835 --> 00:50:48.427
Never mind. What about this?


00:50:48.603 --> 00:50:52.767
Ls this all right? Mass-transit blue?


00:50:57.279 --> 00:50:59.747
When I was locked up,
they had me work in the kitchen.


00:50:59.914 --> 00:51:02.348
So one day a little dude
walk up to me and say:


00:51:02.517 --> 00:51:04.485
"Hey, you think
you could bake me a cake?"


00:51:04.653 --> 00:51:06.416
I said, "Yeah, I'll bake you a cake. "


00:51:06.588 --> 00:51:09.648
I ain't tell him I ain't never
baked a cake, you know.


00:51:09.824 --> 00:51:11.348
But I ain't got shit else to do.


00:51:11.526 --> 00:51:15.462
So, you know, I read the instructions...


00:51:15.630 --> 00:51:18.394
.. I bake him a cake, you know,
for his daughter's birthday.


00:51:18.566 --> 00:51:20.295
She'd come up there to visit him.


00:51:20.468 --> 00:51:24.461
You know, it say,
"Happy Birthday, Angel," right?


00:51:25.073 --> 00:51:27.803
He go crazy.
He can't get enough, you know.


00:51:27.976 --> 00:51:31.503
He said, "Eddie, you done hooked me up.
Man, you the man. "


00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:34.171
And I started doing that.
It was good. I had a skill.


00:51:34.349 --> 00:51:36.510
People look at me different.
They would start...


00:51:36.685 --> 00:51:38.778
- You missed a button.
- Did I?


00:51:38.953 --> 00:51:41.046
Your buttons are all crooked.


00:51:41.222 --> 00:51:43.588
- Come on. Come on, man.
- All right.


00:51:44.392 --> 00:51:46.087
Nugent.


00:51:48.863 --> 00:51:50.694
You're a prince.


00:51:53.301 --> 00:51:56.532
- The word is 5E, boys, 5E.
- Got it.


00:51:59.541 --> 00:52:02.066
Then I start doing my research,
doing my due diligence.


00:52:02.243 --> 00:52:06.339
I found out, you know, it's good money
in birthday cakes for kids, you know.


00:52:06.681 --> 00:52:11.948
That type of thing, like Tweety Bird
or Bugs Bunny or something like that.


00:52:12.120 --> 00:52:14.179
Or Yu-Gi-Oh!.
You ever heard of Yu-Gi-Oh!?


00:52:15.290 --> 00:52:19.249
- Yu-Gi-Oh!.
- Yu-Gi-Oh!. Kids love that, man.


00:52:23.898 --> 00:52:27.163
You don't know Yu-Gi-Oh!?
You gotta get out more. Yu-Gi-Oh! hot.


00:52:27.335 --> 00:52:28.563
Know what I'm saying?


00:52:33.408 --> 00:52:37.242
I'm gonna make money, Jack.
Open up my bakery.


00:52:37.412 --> 00:52:41.405
You gonna eat your words about me, Jack.
How do I look? Do I look all right?


00:52:41.583 --> 00:52:44.882
- All right.
- Freeze! Police!


00:52:45.053 --> 00:52:47.385
- Police! Police!
- Shut up!


00:52:47.555 --> 00:52:49.079
- Oh, my God!
- Shut up!


00:52:50.458 --> 00:52:52.551
Frank, they gave us
the wrong apartment.


00:52:56.731 --> 00:52:58.255
Put it down.


00:52:59.667 --> 00:53:01.601
Put it down.


00:53:06.655 --> 00:53:08.088
Can't get lucky all the time.


00:53:08.523 --> 00:53:10.354
You can be smart every day, though.


00:53:13.261 --> 00:53:16.253
- All right, give me the gun.
- Hold on.


00:53:16.431 --> 00:53:18.296
What are you doing?


00:53:23.939 --> 00:53:25.804
This place is crawling with cops, Eddie.


00:53:26.508 --> 00:53:28.738
Hey, look at me.


00:53:30.545 --> 00:53:33.605
Eddie, what are you doing?


00:53:33.915 --> 00:53:36.383
How does it feel?


00:53:39.754 --> 00:53:41.221
How does it feel?


00:53:41.723 --> 00:53:43.714
You're a baker, right?


00:53:44.726 --> 00:53:47.889
Eddie, listen to him.


00:53:48.196 --> 00:53:50.187
Pull that trigger,
you go to jail for life.


00:53:51.166 --> 00:53:52.565
Frank, we're on our way down.


00:53:53.935 --> 00:53:56.301
Frank, do you read me?


00:54:00.008 --> 00:54:02.169
- You can't stop me, you understand?
- Time to go.


00:54:02.344 --> 00:54:05.279
- Time to go.
- You can't stop me.


00:54:07.482 --> 00:54:09.677
You gave him a loaded weapon?


00:54:13.788 --> 00:54:15.585
- Frank.
- Bobby, get these things off me.


00:54:15.757 --> 00:54:18.351
- Did he take your gun?
- They went south. Get out of here.


00:54:18.526 --> 00:54:22.826
Ortiz! Ortiz, give me a piece.
Give me a piece! Get over here.


00:54:27.302 --> 00:54:29.634
Make a hole, make a hole.
Come on, make a hole.


00:54:42.717 --> 00:54:45.413
Speak to me.
Come on, somebody, speak to me.


00:54:48.723 --> 00:54:50.190
Turn.


00:54:58.400 --> 00:55:00.197
- Excuse me!
- Open up!


00:55:01.202 --> 00:55:03.568
- Excuse me!
- Open up!


00:55:04.406 --> 00:55:06.431
Keep moving. Go.
Go, go, go.


00:55:08.810 --> 00:55:10.038
Oh, shit.


00:55:13.048 --> 00:55:15.346
On the bus! Let's go.


00:55:20.789 --> 00:55:22.586
- Just keep driving.
- What are you doing?


00:55:22.757 --> 00:55:26.215
- I'm a cop. Lock the back door.
- He's got a gun!


00:55:27.729 --> 00:55:30.425
No stops.
Tell them to hang on to something, Eddie!


00:55:30.598 --> 00:55:34.694
Hang on! Don't worry, this man,
he's a police officer.


00:55:34.869 --> 00:55:36.894
- Everything is gonna be fine.
- Hang on!


00:55:37.072 --> 00:55:38.903
Everybody just hang on. Don't worry!


00:55:47.916 --> 00:55:49.508
Right, right, right! Go right!


00:55:54.522 --> 00:55:56.752
- What are you doing?
- Stop this thing!


00:56:08.937 --> 00:56:10.564
Get down!


00:56:37.298 --> 00:56:40.267
Get away from the bus!
Away from the bus!


00:56:43.004 --> 00:56:44.767
Stay down! Stay down!


00:56:50.979 --> 00:56:52.412
Heads down!


00:56:55.283 --> 00:56:57.877
- Where the hell are you?
- Construction site at Baxter.


00:56:58.052 --> 00:56:59.280
He has hostages.


00:57:03.758 --> 00:57:05.020
Let me go.


00:57:13.101 --> 00:57:14.363
Listen!


00:57:14.669 --> 00:57:17.763
Everybody, stand up.
They're not gonna shoot you.


00:57:17.939 --> 00:57:20.339
Stand up in front of the windows.


00:57:20.508 --> 00:57:22.942
They won't shoot you.
You, stay down. Stay down.


00:57:28.116 --> 00:57:30.710
Fill in the blanks. Fill in the spots.


00:57:30.885 --> 00:57:33.012
Scoot over, scoot over! That's it.


00:57:33.188 --> 00:57:36.123
- All right, get Gruber down here.
- Okay.


00:57:41.796 --> 00:57:43.286
Hey!


00:57:44.265 --> 00:57:45.823
All right, seal off that end.


00:57:58.680 --> 00:58:01.979
- It's a busload.
- Jesus, this shit just gets deeper.


00:58:02.150 --> 00:58:03.811
- Bobby?
- Gruber's on his way.


00:58:04.352 --> 00:58:07.344
All right. We gotta get
our stories straight, all right?


00:58:07.522 --> 00:58:09.149
We're getting our stories straight?


00:58:15.063 --> 00:58:16.826
Yeah, suit up.


00:58:28.142 --> 00:58:31.043
Thought we could handle this quickly
and quietly, commissioner.


00:58:31.212 --> 00:58:33.840
A guy shoots a cop,
takes a grand-jury witness hostage...


00:58:34.015 --> 00:58:35.676
.. and we're supposed to make nice?


00:58:35.850 --> 00:58:40.014
Commissioner, look, sir, this is...
Watch your back, sir.


00:58:40.188 --> 00:58:42.053
This is my fault, all right?


00:58:42.223 --> 00:58:45.556
I used to work with Mosley,
so I asked the captain to let me handle it.


00:58:45.727 --> 00:58:49.219
I felt that I could bring him in.
I just didn't realize how far gone he was.


00:58:49.397 --> 00:58:52.958
- Stay on Tac 2, boys.
- Wait for command, here we go.


00:58:54.669 --> 00:58:56.136
That's it, cover them up.


00:58:58.573 --> 00:59:02.236
Good, okay. Great job. Thank you.


00:59:09.584 --> 00:59:12.348
- Commissioner, sir. Captain.
- Hi, Mike.


00:59:12.520 --> 00:59:15.489
- What do we got?
- Cop. Twenty plus, flipped.


00:59:15.657 --> 00:59:18.182
- Suicidal?
- Been to the farm twice the last four years.


00:59:18.359 --> 00:59:20.327
- Twice?
- Twice. Nothing like this, though.


00:59:20.495 --> 00:59:23.521
- What do you know, detective?
- Like the captain said, he flipped.


00:59:23.698 --> 00:59:27.099
After he nailed Shue, he started
spouting crap about making headlines.


00:59:27.268 --> 00:59:29.498
There's no way
that you're getting this guy out.


00:59:30.204 --> 00:59:34.072
Please fall back behind the barricades.
On the sidewalk.


00:59:34.776 --> 00:59:36.266
Smart cop.


00:59:36.711 --> 00:59:40.579
Okay. You're all gonna be okay.
We're gonna get you out of here.


00:59:40.748 --> 00:59:43.615
- Please, just move to the back of the bus.
- Jack?


00:59:43.785 --> 00:59:46.185
Just move to the back of the bus,
please, right now.


00:59:46.354 --> 00:59:49.255
It's okay. You're gonna get off the bus.
I am a police officer.


00:59:49.424 --> 00:59:53.121
Jack, it's Mike Sheehan from HNT.


00:59:53.294 --> 00:59:57.196
We worked that barricade deal
on the concourse a few years ago.


00:59:58.633 --> 01:00:01.625
I'm gonna put this thing down, okay?


01:00:06.240 --> 01:00:08.105
- I'm sorry.
- Jack!


01:00:08.276 --> 01:00:10.870
I'm sorry that I got you
in this situation.


01:00:11.045 --> 01:00:12.979
You know the drill, no weapons.


01:00:14.515 --> 01:00:15.846
Listen, you're on the job.


01:00:16.284 --> 01:00:18.479
- Just keep your head down.
- You know the deal.


01:00:18.653 --> 01:00:21.178
I'm just gonna step in here,
nice and easy...


01:00:21.789 --> 01:00:25.452
.. and hand you this phone
so we can talk, okay?


01:00:25.626 --> 01:00:31.030
Make sure we got no injuries in there.
Jack, just open the door, okay?


01:00:32.867 --> 01:00:34.391
- I need to...
- Just throw it, Mike!


01:00:34.569 --> 01:00:35.900
- Okay, you got it.
- Throw it!


01:00:36.070 --> 01:00:40.302
Here you go. Jack...


01:00:46.280 --> 01:00:47.872
Jack, can you hear me?


01:00:48.583 --> 01:00:50.517
How many people you got in there, Jack?


01:00:51.619 --> 01:00:53.951
Count how many people are here.


01:00:54.889 --> 01:00:57.881
Everybody put your hands up, please.


01:00:58.493 --> 01:01:02.486
N. Y.P.D., we got a situation here.
We need you people back on the sidewalk.


01:01:02.663 --> 01:01:06.565
- Stay behind the barricade.
- Twenty-six, 28. Okay, thank you.


01:01:06.734 --> 01:01:09.362
That's everybody?
Please, don't cry, don't cry.


01:01:09.537 --> 01:01:14.804
Everything's gonna be all right, just relax.
Stay calm, okay? Thank you.


01:01:14.976 --> 01:01:17.035
- What is it?
- Thirty-one. Thirty-one.


01:01:18.546 --> 01:01:24.382
Okay, we have about
40 people on the bus.


01:01:24.786 --> 01:01:26.913
Okay, that's good.


01:01:27.288 --> 01:01:30.223
You know, it's important
that we're clear with each other, Jack.


01:01:30.658 --> 01:01:33.752
ESU and HNT are in place.


01:01:35.997 --> 01:01:39.433
The block is sealed, Jack.
It's a frozen zone.


01:01:39.734 --> 01:01:44.467
So let's work this out
so everybody can go home, all right?


01:01:44.639 --> 01:01:48.302
That's all we wanna do.
Just end it, nice and easy.


01:01:49.477 --> 01:01:50.944
Jack?


01:01:51.112 --> 01:01:53.979
Jack? This is as far as you go, buddy.


01:01:54.315 --> 01:01:55.304
Keep talk...


01:02:14.168 --> 01:02:17.069
- Is everybody okay?
- Yeah.


01:02:17.772 --> 01:02:19.865
- Hi, how are you?
- Good.


01:02:20.041 --> 01:02:21.906
How are you?


01:02:22.076 --> 01:02:27.275
My name's Eddie. Hi, how you doing?
Everybody's okay?


01:02:31.352 --> 01:02:32.819
What's your name?


01:02:33.187 --> 01:02:35.655
- Christina.
- Christina.


01:02:35.923 --> 01:02:40.690
That's a pretty name.
How old are you, Christina?


01:02:42.430 --> 01:02:44.796
- Seven.
- Seven years old.


01:02:47.502 --> 01:02:50.471
And my strawberry recipe...
I know I got one. Let me see.


01:02:51.339 --> 01:02:54.206
Where's my strawberry recipe? Let's see.


01:02:54.976 --> 01:02:58.503
Angel-food-cake recipe right here.


01:02:59.580 --> 01:03:02.981
Here we go, strawberry fan.


01:03:03.718 --> 01:03:05.811
See right here on the top?


01:03:06.120 --> 01:03:07.951
I can put a fan on the top.


01:03:08.623 --> 01:03:12.491
You know, like a Chinese fan?


01:03:12.860 --> 01:03:14.987
I could do that.


01:03:16.030 --> 01:03:17.793
When's your birthday?


01:03:18.232 --> 01:03:22.032
- September 22nd.
- Oh, so that's soon.


01:03:22.203 --> 01:03:26.970
Gonna be 8 years old, huh?
That's gonna be a good day for you.


01:03:27.308 --> 01:03:28.832
When's your birthday?


01:03:30.378 --> 01:03:32.642
Today, actually.


01:03:33.014 --> 01:03:36.415
- Yeah.
- Happy birthday to you.


01:03:40.755 --> 01:03:44.213
And, yeah, every day
is somebody's birthday, you know.


01:03:44.392 --> 01:03:47.555
That's gonna be the motto for my shop:


01:03:47.728 --> 01:03:49.787
"Every day's a birthday," you know.


01:03:49.964 --> 01:03:53.900
I didn't know my birthday
was gonna turn out like this, but...


01:03:54.068 --> 01:03:58.869
Yeah, I'm glad to be, you know,
here, alive, you know.


01:04:01.275 --> 01:04:03.175
- Right here, Jack.
- Yeah, Sheehan.


01:04:03.644 --> 01:04:05.009
Commissioner, sir.


01:04:05.179 --> 01:04:06.976
- Sheehan?
- Right here.


01:04:07.148 --> 01:04:09.673
All right. This is what I want.


01:04:09.850 --> 01:04:13.081
I want you to get me
Assistant District Attorney MacDonald...


01:04:13.254 --> 01:04:17.054
.. a court stenographer
and somebody from TV.


01:04:17.225 --> 01:04:19.022
Somebody that I would recognize.


01:04:19.193 --> 01:04:21.855
I want them to come on the bus
and record sworn testimony.


01:04:22.029 --> 01:04:26.261
When I get what I want,
I'll let everybody out. Safely.


01:04:26.434 --> 01:04:31.269
- That's a tall order. It'll take some time...
- Just do it. I'm not in the mood, okay?


01:04:31.439 --> 01:04:33.737
Get these people here in 15 minutes...


01:04:33.908 --> 01:04:36.433
...or I'm gonna shoot
these passengers one at a time...


01:04:36.611 --> 01:04:39.079
- ... and throw them out the door.
- Jack, be cool, okay?


01:04:39.247 --> 01:04:42.216
Let's not do anything rash.
This thing can end without bloodshed.


01:04:42.383 --> 01:04:44.351
- Okay? We can work this...
- Fifteen minutes.


01:04:44.518 --> 01:04:47.214
Jack? Jack?


01:04:50.391 --> 01:04:52.188
He's gone.


01:04:54.061 --> 01:04:55.653
All right, everybody on your feet.


01:04:57.131 --> 01:05:00.100
- Jack, what are you doing?
- Gotta get these people off this bus.


01:05:00.268 --> 01:05:03.533
But you just made your call.
You called the DA. They said they'd come.


01:05:03.704 --> 01:05:06.002
- Everybody's coming.
- Nobody's coming, okay?


01:05:06.173 --> 01:05:07.731
What do you mean,
nobody's coming?


01:05:07.908 --> 01:05:11.139
They're gonna breach this bus
in less than five minutes.


01:05:11.312 --> 01:05:14.440
- They're gonna kill me, kill you...
- Jack, what about testifying?


01:05:14.615 --> 01:05:16.913
We're right here. We can go.
We can end this.


01:05:17.084 --> 01:05:19.518
- We can testify.
- Nobody's testifying.


01:05:20.521 --> 01:05:22.614
It's all over, Eddie.


01:05:22.790 --> 01:05:24.985
We lose, kid.


01:05:37.038 --> 01:05:39.768
- Hey, Ray.
- Frank.


01:05:39.940 --> 01:05:41.532
You?


01:05:43.210 --> 01:05:44.507
You guys going in?


01:05:44.679 --> 01:05:47.113
The commissioner hasn't given us
the green light yet.


01:05:47.281 --> 01:05:53.277
Well, I don't need to remind you
that he shot two of us.


01:05:55.323 --> 01:05:57.257
Enough said.


01:05:57.725 --> 01:06:00.626
We got maybe 40 civilians on that bus.
Get them out.


01:06:00.795 --> 01:06:02.888
I don't want anybody hurt,
including our guys.


01:06:03.064 --> 01:06:06.158
Nobody's gonna get hurt, commissioner.
These guys know what to do.


01:06:13.374 --> 01:06:15.899
- We have movement.
- Let's move in.


01:06:16.077 --> 01:06:18.910
- Hold your fire. Repeat, hold your fire.
- Move in to the bus. Let's go.


01:06:21.916 --> 01:06:23.679
Hey. What...?


01:06:25.653 --> 01:06:26.642
Bob.


01:06:29.523 --> 01:06:30.717
When you get outside...


01:06:30.891 --> 01:06:32.756
- Happy birthday.
- Thank you.


01:06:32.927 --> 01:06:35.589
They'll take you to a holding area.
It'll be hectic.


01:06:35.763 --> 01:06:38.664
- But everybody's out there...
- Listen to me, listen to me.


01:06:38.833 --> 01:06:41.393
Once you get outside that perimeter,
you just get lost.


01:06:41.569 --> 01:06:44.561
- What if they...?
- Keep moving. You just keep moving.


01:06:44.739 --> 01:06:46.070
Come here. You look great.


01:06:46.240 --> 01:06:48.003
Hey, gray suit.


01:06:49.143 --> 01:06:50.667
Got you a gray suit.


01:06:50.845 --> 01:06:54.042
All right? Hands in the air, folks.
Don't look back.


01:07:02.123 --> 01:07:05.058
Hands in the air, you'll be all right.
You'll be all right.


01:07:17.271 --> 01:07:18.795
Next. Sorry.


01:07:28.582 --> 01:07:30.447
Come on, come on, let's go!


01:07:30.618 --> 01:07:32.449
- What is he doing?
- How should I know?


01:07:32.620 --> 01:07:34.713
- I'll let you know when I know.
- Don't you...


01:07:34.889 --> 01:07:37.255
I'll let you know when I know.
Out of my face!


01:07:47.435 --> 01:07:49.733
Kaller, give me a hand with them!


01:07:53.874 --> 01:07:56.240
Bobby? Right there. Right here.


01:07:56.777 --> 01:07:59.473
- That's him. That's him.
- Hey, man!


01:08:00.581 --> 01:08:02.708
- It's not him.
- Let him go.


01:08:02.883 --> 01:08:04.942
- The dude, he changed. It's not me.
- What?


01:08:05.119 --> 01:08:07.781
- He's in a suit, a gray suit.
- Suit, gray suit.


01:08:28.709 --> 01:08:31.371
- We count 31.
- That leaves eight people on the bus.


01:08:31.545 --> 01:08:33.206
No, I was the last one off the bus.


01:08:33.380 --> 01:08:36.281
The only person left on that bus
is the guy with the gun.


01:08:37.351 --> 01:08:39.182
- Then go, do it!
- Let's go, let's go.


01:08:39.353 --> 01:08:42.584
- Get your people out there. Let's go.
- Come on, let's go.


01:08:43.390 --> 01:08:46.518
Mosley is still on the bus.
That kid is here somewhere. We checked...


01:08:46.694 --> 01:08:48.491
Bobby, I don't care what you checked.


01:08:48.662 --> 01:08:51.222
Check it again, now. Go.
You guys, that way.


01:09:05.045 --> 01:09:10.005
This is Detective Jack Mosley.
Shield number 227.


01:09:21.028 --> 01:09:23.588
I guess this will be
my last will and testament.


01:10:17.418 --> 01:10:18.646
Don't shoot!


01:10:19.019 --> 01:10:20.418
Hold your fire!


01:10:20.588 --> 01:10:22.385
Do not shoot! Do not shoot!


01:10:22.556 --> 01:10:24.751
- Who is that?
- Hold your fire!


01:10:25.559 --> 01:10:27.618
- Hold your fire!
- Is it that wit from the 32?


01:10:29.229 --> 01:10:31.493
Get on your goddamn radio.
Find out who that is.


01:10:31.665 --> 01:10:33.428
Guns down, hold your fire!


01:10:34.969 --> 01:10:36.197
Don't shoot!


01:10:36.370 --> 01:10:38.304
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!


01:10:40.407 --> 01:10:41.669
Don't shoot!


01:10:41.842 --> 01:10:43.605
Don't shoot!


01:10:47.081 --> 01:10:50.482
- Do not move! Step away from the bus!
- Don't shoot, hold your fire!


01:10:50.651 --> 01:10:52.642
- Do not shoot!
- Get away from the bus!


01:10:52.820 --> 01:10:53.946
Hold your fire.


01:10:54.955 --> 01:10:58.823
Jack. Jack, it's me. Jack Mosley!


01:10:59.460 --> 01:11:01.360
Lt's me, Eddie, Jack.


01:11:04.198 --> 01:11:05.597
Chuck Berry.


01:11:05.933 --> 01:11:07.423
Chuck Berry.


01:11:07.901 --> 01:11:11.428
Chuck Berry,
he got locked up for armed robbery.


01:11:11.605 --> 01:11:13.869
He changed. He changed.


01:11:15.609 --> 01:11:19.136
Barry White, he stole 300 tires.


01:11:19.313 --> 01:11:24.444
Can you picture big Barry White
stealing 300 tires? He changed.


01:11:24.618 --> 01:11:26.984
You said... You said people don't change.


01:11:27.554 --> 01:11:29.954
- People change.
- Eddie.


01:11:30.691 --> 01:11:33.057
- What?
- You're killing me.


01:11:33.327 --> 01:11:37.058
Team three, breach the bus.
Repeat, team three, breach the bus.


01:11:37.231 --> 01:11:39.699
Entrance team moving in.


01:11:52.813 --> 01:11:55.304
Get out of the way!


01:11:56.150 --> 01:11:58.744
Head down!
Cover your ears and your eyes!


01:12:04.324 --> 01:12:05.552
- Hold fire.
- Go, go!


01:12:05.959 --> 01:12:08.018
- Go, go, go!
- Hold your fire!


01:12:08.195 --> 01:12:09.219
This is a nightmare.


01:12:26.113 --> 01:12:27.444
Hold fire!


01:12:58.979 --> 01:13:00.776
- Let's go! Move, move, move!
- Stay down!


01:13:00.948 --> 01:13:02.415
- Move up! Move up!
- Come here.


01:13:02.583 --> 01:13:05.313
Team two, status?


01:13:05.486 --> 01:13:08.580
Go ahead! Take it! Go!


01:13:39.186 --> 01:13:41.450
The bus is empty.


01:13:41.622 --> 01:13:43.317
They went through the bus doors!


01:13:43.490 --> 01:13:47.119
They're in the goddamn building!
Seal it off!


01:13:47.795 --> 01:13:50.662
- All clear. The bus is empty.
- They've entered the building.


01:13:53.000 --> 01:13:54.592
Seal the building, start a search.


01:13:54.768 --> 01:13:57.236
Remember, heads up.
He just shot two cops. Be careful.


01:13:59.573 --> 01:14:01.473
Jack, I gotta tell you something.


01:14:01.642 --> 01:14:04.042
Hey, man. Jack, listen to me, man.


01:14:04.211 --> 01:14:06.270
Jack, I wanna tell you something.


01:14:06.446 --> 01:14:10.143
Hold on, hold on, wait.
I gotta tell you something. It's important.


01:14:10.684 --> 01:14:13.152
Shit. Get up, go.


01:14:15.355 --> 01:14:17.255
Oh, shit.


01:14:18.425 --> 01:14:20.825
Hey, sir. I'm a cop, all right?
I'm on the job.


01:14:20.994 --> 01:14:23.019
Look, I need that phone for a minute.


01:14:23.197 --> 01:14:24.789
Look what you did to my suit, man.


01:14:25.332 --> 01:14:27.960
I told you you was gonna get me shot.


01:14:28.969 --> 01:14:30.402
It's me. I need your help.


01:14:30.838 --> 01:14:34.934
All this started because my friend
Maurice came by my house.


01:14:36.710 --> 01:14:40.168
Two days ago,
Maurice came by my house.


01:14:40.347 --> 01:14:41.746
He all excited.


01:14:41.915 --> 01:14:44.509
He got a shoebox.


01:14:44.685 --> 01:14:45.982
He had a gun.


01:14:46.153 --> 01:14:48.713
He talking about,
"Hold this for me for a little while. "


01:14:48.889 --> 01:14:52.655
I'm like, "I'm on parole. "
He like, "Me too. "


01:14:52.826 --> 01:14:56.762
Next day, somebody shot him.


01:14:58.065 --> 01:15:00.590
Thirty-two thousand dollars
in that shoebox.


01:15:02.703 --> 01:15:05.433
- That's a sign, huh?
- Yeah.


01:15:05.606 --> 01:15:07.836
It's a very big sign.


01:15:08.008 --> 01:15:10.533
Easy, easy, easy.


01:15:14.481 --> 01:15:18.850
You know how much it gonna take me
to open the bakery?


01:15:21.255 --> 01:15:23.780
Thirty-one thousand dollars.


01:15:23.957 --> 01:15:28.690
Jack, I got so nervous
I ran out the house.


01:15:28.862 --> 01:15:33.390
I went to Port Authority
and I put the money in a locker.


01:15:37.471 --> 01:15:38.733
I get back to my house...


01:15:38.906 --> 01:15:41.238
.. my parole officer's there...


01:15:41.408 --> 01:15:43.035
.. in my house.


01:15:43.210 --> 01:15:46.043
He got Maurice's gun in his hand.


01:15:46.213 --> 01:15:49.478
He looking at me like, "That's it, Eddie. "


01:15:49.816 --> 01:15:51.716
And he's talking about 15 years, man.


01:15:52.286 --> 01:15:54.254
I got so sick.


01:15:54.421 --> 01:15:57.982
Then the DA came to my cell...


01:15:59.459 --> 01:16:02.485
.. and he showed me
the picture of that cop.


01:16:03.997 --> 01:16:05.828
Then I met you.


01:16:06.366 --> 01:16:11.269
Jack, they clean them lockers out
every 24 hours.


01:16:12.706 --> 01:16:14.731
I had a little schedule going, man.


01:16:16.109 --> 01:16:18.509
Court at 10:00...


01:16:19.546 --> 01:16:21.810
.. Port Authority at 12.


01:16:21.982 --> 01:16:23.973
Hey. Hey, look at me. Wake up.


01:16:24.818 --> 01:16:26.752
You ain't gonna die on me, are you?


01:16:28.922 --> 01:16:31.584
I don't know, I never died before.


01:16:31.758 --> 01:16:34.056
It's not gonna happen today.


01:16:44.137 --> 01:16:45.627
Hey. Thank you for coming.


01:16:45.806 --> 01:16:50.641
- What's going on?
- Look. Shot here. I think it went in and out.


01:16:51.011 --> 01:16:52.842
Yeah, let's get him in.


01:16:55.082 --> 01:16:56.515
I know you.


01:16:56.683 --> 01:16:58.548
- Come on.
- I was at your house.


01:16:58.719 --> 01:17:00.812
- You were at my apartment?
- Had to get my gun.


01:17:00.988 --> 01:17:02.853
Bigmouth.


01:17:03.423 --> 01:17:06.790
It was very nice, very clean.


01:17:07.861 --> 01:17:10.329
The police grilled me
for an hour at the hospital.


01:17:10.497 --> 01:17:11.725
What'd you say to them?


01:17:11.898 --> 01:17:14.298
That you're a self-medicating,
depressed individual.


01:17:14.468 --> 01:17:16.629
And you don't care
about anything or anyone.


01:17:16.803 --> 01:17:21.297
Oh, she's honest, straightforward.
That's sexy. I like that.


01:17:30.884 --> 01:17:32.408
What'd you do this time, Jack?


01:17:32.586 --> 01:17:35.350
He saved my life a couple times.


01:17:36.656 --> 01:17:41.525
Hey, he's a good dude.
You gotta give him another chance.


01:17:41.695 --> 01:17:44.630
I don't know what he did,
but you gotta give him another chance.


01:17:44.798 --> 01:17:47.232
He gotta have somebody to talk to.


01:17:47.401 --> 01:17:49.926
I'm not gonna be around.


01:17:51.838 --> 01:17:55.433
- Eddie, this is my sister, Diane.
- What?


01:17:56.076 --> 01:17:58.169
She's your sister?


01:17:58.745 --> 01:18:00.576
Oh, man.


01:18:00.747 --> 01:18:04.444
I just started having a little hope for you.
Your family don't even like you.


01:18:04.618 --> 01:18:07.280
I got a sister too.


01:18:08.355 --> 01:18:11.085
But she live in Seattle.


01:18:11.258 --> 01:18:13.692
I was supposed to go out there
and start my bakery.


01:18:13.860 --> 01:18:16.385
I was supposed to go out there today
to see her.


01:18:16.563 --> 01:18:18.554
See her on the bus.


01:18:19.299 --> 01:18:20.527
I can stop the bleeding...


01:18:20.700 --> 01:18:23.191
.. but he's gotta get stitched up,
get to a hospital.


01:18:23.703 --> 01:18:25.796
We gotta be at the courthouse
in less than 20.


01:18:26.306 --> 01:18:28.467
You're gonna have to do it.


01:18:32.012 --> 01:18:34.708
You're gonna be fine, Eddie.
It's not as bad as it looks.


01:18:36.983 --> 01:18:38.746
What happened to your hand?


01:18:40.487 --> 01:18:42.478
I gotta ask you one more favor.


01:18:44.391 --> 01:18:46.916
Just a little favor.


01:18:53.800 --> 01:18:56.098
Hey, is today really your birthday?


01:18:56.269 --> 01:18:57.930
No.


01:18:58.105 --> 01:19:02.701
No, I just said that because the little girl,
she was so scared.


01:19:03.410 --> 01:19:05.605
She was cute, man.


01:19:06.513 --> 01:19:08.447
When's your birthday?


01:19:10.984 --> 01:19:13.817
- I don't know.
- What do you mean, you don't know?


01:19:15.789 --> 01:19:18.485
No, for real, I don't know.


01:19:18.658 --> 01:19:22.594
I'm not... I came up in foster care.
Had a lot of birthdays.


01:19:22.762 --> 01:19:27.597
But didn't you say...? You got a sister, right?
That you're going to see?


01:19:27.767 --> 01:19:30.759
Yeah, I just found out about her
a couple months ago.


01:19:30.937 --> 01:19:32.996
- Never met your sister?
- No.


01:19:34.574 --> 01:19:37.407
That's why I'm going out to Seattle
to meet her.


01:19:38.512 --> 01:19:39.809
I'm looking forward.


01:19:39.980 --> 01:19:42.778
Maybe she turns out
to look like Angelina Jolie.


01:19:42.949 --> 01:19:46.214
Shit, if she do,
I hope she ain't my sister.


01:19:50.590 --> 01:19:52.888
Hey, man, what you want
on your cake, man?


01:19:53.059 --> 01:19:55.220
You never told me.
I gotta send you one, man.


01:19:56.363 --> 01:19:59.230
- I don't want no cake, Eddie.
- Damn it, Jack, come on, man...


01:19:59.399 --> 01:20:01.993
I can't think of anything
that has happened in my life...


01:20:02.169 --> 01:20:05.229
.. that I would want written on a cake.
- Nothing?


01:20:07.374 --> 01:20:09.308
I'm not a good guy, Eddie.


01:20:14.514 --> 01:20:16.641
I'm not a good guy.


01:20:20.487 --> 01:20:22.318
Yeah, me neither.


01:20:36.937 --> 01:20:38.165
- Diane.
- Frank.


01:20:38.338 --> 01:20:40.135
Give me the keys.


01:20:40.307 --> 01:20:43.140
- Stay in the car.
- Little out of your sector, aren't you?


01:20:43.310 --> 01:20:44.937
Saving lives knows no bounds.


01:20:45.111 --> 01:20:47.602
- You should know that, Frank.
- You look good.


01:20:47.781 --> 01:20:50.011
You look a little desperate.
Doesn't suit you.


01:20:50.183 --> 01:20:51.650
Open the door.


01:20:51.818 --> 01:20:54.048
Open the door. Open the door.


01:20:55.488 --> 01:20:57.956
Sorry, Jack, this is as close
as I can get you.


01:21:04.564 --> 01:21:06.691
Like I said, you're looking good.


01:21:11.371 --> 01:21:12.929
Thanks, kid.


01:21:14.040 --> 01:21:15.405
All right, come on, let's go.


01:21:15.575 --> 01:21:18.043
No, hey, hold on. Hold on a minute.


01:21:18.211 --> 01:21:19.610
Why is that? Hold on for what?


01:21:19.779 --> 01:21:21.679
This is as far as you go too.


01:21:21.848 --> 01:21:23.975
- Come on, man. I don't...
- Listen to me, Eddie.


01:21:24.150 --> 01:21:26.584
- What?
- Listen.


01:21:27.988 --> 01:21:30.684
Those guys you were gonna
testify against...


01:21:30.857 --> 01:21:32.916
.. those cops?
- Yeah?


01:21:34.394 --> 01:21:35.793
I was one of them.


01:21:44.271 --> 01:21:46.671
You were gonna testify against me too.


01:21:49.309 --> 01:21:51.402
I did what they did.


01:21:51.578 --> 01:21:54.046
We did some bad things.


01:21:55.215 --> 01:21:58.412
I did another bad thing when I used you.


01:21:59.653 --> 01:22:03.851
I was gonna let you do
what I should have done.


01:22:04.024 --> 01:22:07.050
What I should have had the courage
to do six years ago.


01:22:12.499 --> 01:22:13.864
I'm sorry.


01:22:19.005 --> 01:22:23.237
You know, if you didn't
come to get me today...


01:22:24.277 --> 01:22:26.711
.. I'd be dead right now.


01:22:26.880 --> 01:22:28.677
- Right.
- So...


01:22:30.150 --> 01:22:32.744
I was supposed to meet you.


01:22:33.353 --> 01:22:35.583
That was the sign.


01:22:35.989 --> 01:22:38.219
You saved my life, kid.


01:22:43.129 --> 01:22:45.654
Take care of yourself, kid.


01:22:47.567 --> 01:22:48.795
Thank you.


01:22:49.336 --> 01:22:52.499
Make cakes, Eddie the baker.


01:23:00.213 --> 01:23:04.013
Oh, yeah. You give the car keys
to your best friend.


01:23:04.184 --> 01:23:06.880
You let him take the old lady
to the hospital.


01:23:07.053 --> 01:23:11.922
You stay at the bus stop with the girl
because she's the girl of your dreams, right?


01:23:12.092 --> 01:23:14.492
So everything's gonna be okay.


01:23:15.395 --> 01:23:17.363
- Right?
- Yeah.


01:23:18.631 --> 01:23:20.861
Have fun in Seattle. Say hi to your sister.


01:23:21.034 --> 01:23:22.626
Yeah.


01:23:26.873 --> 01:23:28.363
Yeah.


01:23:29.676 --> 01:23:32.474
Get him to the Port Authority.
Make sure he gets on that bus.


01:23:32.645 --> 01:23:33.873
- Carl, thanks.
- No problem.


01:23:34.047 --> 01:23:35.446
All right.


01:24:48.021 --> 01:24:49.682
Hell of a morning, huh?


01:24:59.766 --> 01:25:01.028
Where's the wit?


01:25:03.369 --> 01:25:04.700
You're looking at him.


01:25:08.775 --> 01:25:10.640
I let the kid go, Frank.


01:25:12.011 --> 01:25:15.970
- You're not gonna get to him now.
- Bullshit.


01:25:17.684 --> 01:25:18.946
Wouldn't do that.


01:25:28.695 --> 01:25:30.322
So...


01:25:32.165 --> 01:25:34.156
.. what do you think
you're gonna tell them?


01:25:35.468 --> 01:25:37.561
Are you gonna tell them everything?


01:25:37.737 --> 01:25:40.399
Are you gonna tell them about you too?


01:25:41.975 --> 01:25:44.136
You think that's gonna
make you feel better?


01:25:44.544 --> 01:25:46.273
Nothing's gonna make me feel better.


01:25:46.446 --> 01:25:48.175
Then why?


01:25:49.449 --> 01:25:51.474
Look, Jack, you and me...


01:25:51.651 --> 01:25:56.645
.. we did our business in a certain way.


01:25:58.858 --> 01:26:02.385
You never complained
when we cleared the tough cases.


01:26:02.562 --> 01:26:06.328
It didn't bother you
doing any of that until...


01:26:07.700 --> 01:26:10.430
Listen to me, all right? You listen.


01:26:10.603 --> 01:26:13.504
Okay, Jack? Really listen.


01:26:13.673 --> 01:26:16.574
Whatever you think
that you are gonna do up there...


01:26:17.477 --> 01:26:19.274
.. it is never gonna happen.


01:26:20.246 --> 01:26:22.806
You are not gonna make it.


01:26:24.417 --> 01:26:26.885
Is that what you're thinking, Frank?


01:26:27.420 --> 01:26:31.584
You're gonna shoot me down here?
Nobody knows?


01:26:33.259 --> 01:26:35.853
Like the Ling family, huh?


01:26:36.029 --> 01:26:37.257
Like they never knew.


01:26:37.430 --> 01:26:40.024
He was a stupid old man
who wouldn't keep his mouth shut.


01:26:40.199 --> 01:26:42.724
All right, so I stuck a gun
in some guy's mouth.


01:26:42.902 --> 01:26:46.235
- He had a heart attack, he died. So what?
- So what?


01:26:46.406 --> 01:26:49.603
Look, if it hadn't happened
the way that it did, if he hadn't died...


01:26:49.776 --> 01:26:52.939
.. you would've been patting me
on the back, saying, "Good job. "


01:26:53.112 --> 01:26:55.842
Collateral damage,
it is a fact of life in this business.


01:26:56.015 --> 01:26:59.576
He took his last breaths while you were
wiping the fingerprints off the room.


01:26:59.752 --> 01:27:02.687
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was an innocent man.


01:27:02.855 --> 01:27:06.222
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was somebody's husband.


01:27:06.392 --> 01:27:09.156
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was somebody's father.


01:27:09.329 --> 01:27:12.127
He was gonna take down our case!
What were we supposed to do?


01:27:12.298 --> 01:27:15.631
- He wanted to tell the truth.
- Fuck the truth!


01:27:26.479 --> 01:27:27.912
Right.


01:27:46.966 --> 01:27:49.662
I'm not gonna need this anymore.


01:28:34.295 --> 01:28:36.263
Bobby? He's on his way up.


01:28:37.131 --> 01:28:38.120
Take him out.


01:29:11.566 --> 01:29:14.364
Mosley's in the building!
Get the ADA. Freeze!


01:29:14.535 --> 01:29:16.469
- Hands in the air!
- Don't shoot.


01:29:16.637 --> 01:29:18.798
- Don't move! Down on your knees.
- I'm not armed.


01:29:18.973 --> 01:29:21.703
- Down on your knees! Now!
- Don't shoot, I'm not armed.


01:29:21.876 --> 01:29:25.505
Lower your weapon. Just call
ADA MacDonald, please, on the radio.


01:29:25.680 --> 01:29:28.012
- Hands up.
- Get ADA MacDonald here right now!


01:29:28.182 --> 01:29:30.480
- Don't shoot. Don't shoot me.
- Get your hands up!


01:29:30.651 --> 01:29:32.414
Just get ADA MacDonald for me.


01:29:32.587 --> 01:29:35.385
- Jack, come on!
- I won't argue with you. Get down.


01:29:35.556 --> 01:29:37.353
Mosley! Mosley!


01:29:37.525 --> 01:29:38.787
Hands up!


01:29:38.960 --> 01:29:41.224
Where's my witness?
Where's Edward Bunker?


01:29:41.829 --> 01:29:43.694
He didn't make it.


01:29:44.532 --> 01:29:46.056
I'm gonna take his place.


01:29:51.672 --> 01:29:54.607
- Please lower your weapons.
- Hold your fire and stand down.


01:29:54.775 --> 01:29:56.402
Back off.


01:29:58.579 --> 01:30:00.706
I have information...


01:30:00.881 --> 01:30:04.112
.. regarding your ongoing
witness-tampering investigation.


01:30:04.986 --> 01:30:07.750
Dates, cases that include extortion...


01:30:08.322 --> 01:30:11.348
.. manslaughter and possible homicide...


01:30:12.159 --> 01:30:15.026
.. involving members
of the 14th Precinct.


01:30:16.130 --> 01:30:19.588
These charges include
Captain Dan Gruber...


01:30:19.934 --> 01:30:22.095
.. detectives Jerry Shue...


01:30:22.803 --> 01:30:24.771
.. Edward Maldonado...


01:30:25.539 --> 01:30:27.769
.. Bob Torres...


01:30:27.942 --> 01:30:29.842
.. Jim Mulvey...


01:30:31.145 --> 01:30:32.806
.. myself...


01:30:33.881 --> 01:30:35.610
.. and Detective Frank Nugent.


01:30:39.587 --> 01:30:42.317
What's this about, Mosley?
What do you want?


01:30:43.090 --> 01:30:45.115
I want Edward Bunker's record expunged.


01:30:45.326 --> 01:30:48.557
- Done. What else?
- Nothing else.


01:30:48.729 --> 01:30:50.492
You can substantiate all this, Mosley?


01:30:52.099 --> 01:30:53.566
Yeah.


01:30:54.568 --> 01:30:55.660
Gun!


01:31:01.909 --> 01:31:04.434
Hold your fire. I fired that shot.


01:31:10.251 --> 01:31:13.914
You're gonna shoot me down here?
Nobody knows?


01:31:16.023 --> 01:31:17.650
Like the Ling family, huh?


01:31:18.626 --> 01:31:20.821
Like they never knew.


01:31:20.995 --> 01:31:23.589
He was a stupid old man
who wouldn't keep his mouth shut.


01:31:23.764 --> 01:31:26.198
All right, so I stuck a gun
in some guy's mouth.


01:31:26.367 --> 01:31:29.393
- He had a heart attack, he died. So what?
- So what?


01:31:29.570 --> 01:31:31.663
- So what?
- So how about he was innocent?


01:31:31.839 --> 01:31:34.273
- Innocent?
- How about he didn't deserve to die?


01:31:34.442 --> 01:31:37.934
Look, if it hadn't happened
the way that it did, if he hadn't died...


01:31:38.112 --> 01:31:41.047
...you would've been patting me
on the back, saying, "Good job. "


01:31:41.215 --> 01:31:44.013
Collateral damage,
it is a fact of life in this business.


01:31:44.185 --> 01:31:47.746
He took his last breaths while you were
wiping the fingerprints off the room.


01:31:47.922 --> 01:31:50.584
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was an innocent man.


01:31:50.758 --> 01:31:53.989
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was somebody's husband.


01:31:54.161 --> 01:31:56.925
- He was gonna take down our case.
- He was somebody's father.


01:31:57.098 --> 01:31:59.896
He was gonna take down our case!
What were we supposed to do?


01:32:00.067 --> 01:32:03.059
- He wanted to tell the truth.
- Fuck the truth!


01:32:06.774 --> 01:32:08.935
Let's get you to the jury.


01:32:24.024 --> 01:32:25.048
- Thanks a lot.
- Thanks.


01:32:25.226 --> 01:32:26.488
Okay.


01:32:43.410 --> 01:32:45.776
- Hey, happy birthday.
- Happy birthday, Jack.


01:32:45.946 --> 01:32:48.039
Welcome back, Jack.


01:32:48.215 --> 01:32:50.740
- Are you kidding me?
- Two years in the pen is enough.


01:32:50.918 --> 01:32:52.852
Thanks for that memory. Thank you.


01:32:53.020 --> 01:32:54.851
- Happy birthday, Jack.
- Happy birthday.


01:32:55.022 --> 01:32:57.388
- Happy birthday. Blow them out.
- Welcome home.


01:32:57.558 --> 01:33:00.118
I hate birthdays, you know that, right?


01:33:02.062 --> 01:33:04.724
- Sorry, sorry.
- Happy birthday.


01:33:14.708 --> 01:33:16.505
This came with it.


01:33:28.088 --> 01:33:30.079
Dear Jack Mosley:


01:33:30.257 --> 01:33:34.853
I hope you're doing well and everything
worked out like it was supposed to.


01:33:35.029 --> 01:33:37.054
I'm doing great.


01:33:37.231 --> 01:33:39.222
Seattle is different, and I like it a lot.


01:33:39.400 --> 01:33:43.769
I'm not sure I ever smelled fresh air
before I got here. It's a trip.


01:33:43.938 --> 01:33:47.396
Sometimes I can't believe it.
It's the best feeling I've had in my life.


01:33:48.075 --> 01:33:49.975
I'm busting my ass,
but I'm happy, though.


01:33:53.447 --> 01:33:55.938
The bakery is now open. Three cheers.


01:33:57.751 --> 01:34:00.447
I put my name first
because I'm doing all the hard work.


01:34:00.621 --> 01:34:02.680
These ovens are hot, man.


01:34:02.857 --> 01:34:05.223
Hope you like the cake.
What did I tell you?


01:34:05.392 --> 01:34:09.726
- That's Eddie.
- If you're ever in town, you got a friend.


01:34:09.897 --> 01:34:12.923
Thank you for doing the right thing,
Jack Mosley. God bless you.


01:34:13.434 --> 01:34:17.165
Keep in touch. Peace.


01:34:17.338 --> 01:34:19.568
- That's great.
- Go on, take one more. Look.


01:34:19.740 --> 01:34:24.143
You know how this guy...?
I was talking, take one more.


01:34:25.779 --> 01:34:28.009
Happy birthday, Jack.

